   "source": [
    "# GOAL: Figure out what values to use in the weighting matrix 'w'linear_regression\n",
    "#   Regression formula became \n",
    "#     Xw ≈ y\n",
    "#   So we can cancel out the feature matrix X by multiplying the inverse of X with X\n",
    "#     X⁻¹Xw = X⁻¹y\n",
    "#        Iw = X⁻¹y\n",
    "#         w = X⁻¹y\n",
    "#   However, the feature matrix tends to have many rows and only a few columns\n",
    "#   Inverse matricies must be square\n",
    "# \n",
    "#   In machine learning, the approximation of the inverse matrix is called a GRAM MATRIX\n",
    "#   (The matrix XᵀX is called the GRAM MARTIX and has n+1 rows and n+1 columns)\n",
    "#\n",
    "#            XᵀXw = Xᵀy            # XᵀX will cancel the matrix X \n",
    "#               w = Xᵀy\n",
    "\n",
    "#     (XᵀX)⁻¹XᵀXw = (XᵀX)⁻¹Xᵀy     # (XᵀX)⁻¹XᵀX produces an identity matrix\n",
    "#               w = (XᵀX)⁻¹Xᵀy"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 33,
