   "source": [
    "# SOLUTION IS CALLED 'REGULARIZATION' \n",
    "#   REGULARIZATION reglates the weighting factors\n",
    "#   add a small number to the diagonal of the matrix. \n",
    "#   If we add a small number to the diagonal - say 0.01 - the inverse can still be found, \n",
    "#   and the numbers in it are much more under control. \n",
    "#   The larger the number we add to the diagonal, the more control we get over the weights.\n",
    "\n",
    "# RIDGE REGRESSION\n",
    "#  numpy.eye(NNN) CREATEs AN IDENTITY (eye) MATRIX \n",
    "#   (1's running diagonally across the matrix from cell [0,0],...[n,n] where all other cells have zeros\n",
    "#   regular matrix multiplication (not dot multiplication) by 0.01 will multiply the value in each cell by 0.01\n",
    "#   regular matrix addition can add the values in each element of matrices with the same shape with their corresponding element in another matrix\n",
    "#\n",
    "#   XTX = XTX + (0.01 * np.eye(3))"
   ]
